<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBP-AG19-F002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBP-AG19-F002" ;
  triage:title "Untyped boolean-condition state distinction in the dispatcher" ;
  triage:description "rust-best-practices-agent finding from AG19-REAL-QA-1: DaemonRequestDispatcher::dispatch_send (crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/dispatch_delivery.rs on s18-s20 and integrate) forks ack-vs-send dispatch on the untyped boolean guard request.acknowledges_message_id.is_some() && request.source_remote_host.is_none() instead of a typed enum/classifier. route_send_request()/SendRequestRoute (crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs:271-276,230-233) already demonstrates the typed alternative for the local-vs-remote distinction in the same dispatch path, but the ack-vs-send fork itself was never converted to a type; on s21-s25 it is present verbatim (same untyped boolean guard, same two-outcome fork) but relocated to crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs (execute_outbound_send_with_runtime_and_post_send_emitter). This is the same underlying pattern already tracked ladder-wide as AG18-QA-003 ('Send-vs-ack dispatch fork relocated, not deleted'); RBP-AG19-F002 is the rust-best-practices framing (typed-state-vs-boolean-condition) of the identical code fork AG18-QA-003 already tracks at blocking severity. Full repeatable-pattern sweep executed across all 8 feature branches plus integration branch." ;
  triage:category "RBP" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-19T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
